DATABASE RIGHTS
---------------

Section 4 of the CC BY 4.0 legal code expressly extends the license to sui
generis database rights where they apply. This matters for the curated gene
index in assets/gene_index.json: in the United Kingdom, the European Union, and
other jurisdictions that recognise database rights separately from copyright,
a permissive software licence alone would not clearly grant reuse of the
collection itself. CC BY 4.0 closes that gap.

The gene index is intended to be reused, corrected, and extended. If you build
on it, attribution plus a note of what you changed is all that is asked.


IF YOU MODIFY THE CLINICAL CONTENT
----------------------------------

Indicating changes is a licence condition, and here it is also a safety matter.
The reference files encode guardrails — the three-tier risk policy, the
secondary-findings routing, the rule against reciting surveillance specifics
from memory. If you alter any of these, say so prominently, so that downstream
users know they are not running the reviewed version.


